        <content type="html" xml:base="https://sacanthias.github.io/projects/eclogue/">&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-it-is&quot;&gt;What It Is&lt;&#x2F;h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drover is a single-player environmental adventure game, where the player dons the role of a sheepdog attempting to guide a single sheep through a treacherous forest back to the main herd. Along the way, the two encounter obstacles and hostile wildlife, which they must avoid to return home.&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This was an academic project for the course IGME 320 - Game Design and Development II, which I took for&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;img class=&quot;w-100 mb-2&quot; src=&quot;{{cover.colocated_path}}&quot;&gt;
&lt;h1 id=&quot;development&quot;&gt;Development&lt;&#x2F;h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drover is a single-player&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;to display our game at RIT&#x27;s &lt;a href=&quot;https:&#x2F;&#x2F;sacanthias.github.io&#x2F;projects&#x2F;eclogue&#x2F;www.rit.edu&#x2F;computing&#x2F;school-interactive-games-and-media&#x2F;ims&quot;&gt;Interactive Media Symposium&lt;&#x2F;a&gt;.&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Some of the work I&#x27;ve done with Drover involve the designing and implementation of various menus in the game, such as the start screen and pause menus, the design and process of which I discuss more in depth in &lt;a href=&quot;https:&#x2F;&#x2F;sacanthias.github.io&#x2F;blog&#x2F;eclogue-menus-design&#x2F;&quot;&gt;this&lt;&#x2F;a&gt; blog post.&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
